{"agent":"fx-phase-deps","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new logic does not implement the documented `docs_ignore_phase_needs` contract. For `[gates].doc_globs = [\"docs/**\"]` and a docs-only task with `globs = [\"docs/**/*.md\"]`, the line `if \"**\" in glob: return False` makes `_glob_is_docs` return `False` because the task glob contains `**` and is not literally in `doc_globs`. Every path matching `docs/**/*.md` is under `docs/**` and therefore a document per the config, but the task still inherits the phase's `needs` and remains blocked.","digest":"49c9a2c8a3d552c4","location":"ddflow/core/schedule.py:_glob_is_docs","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/schedule.py:_glob_is_docs"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The `*`/`?` probe is not a sound inclusion test. With `[gates].doc_globs = [\"docs/x*\"]` and a task glob `docs/*`, the probe is `docs/x`; `path_in_glob(\"docs/x\", \"docs/x*\")` is true, so `_docs_only_exempt` skips phase dependencies. But `docs/*` also matches `docs/y`, which is not in `doc_globs`; hence a task that can write non-doc files is incorrectly exempted from `phase.needs`.","digest":"98cea9a4195864be","location":"ddflow/core/schedule.py:_glob_is_docs","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/schedule.py:_glob_is_docs"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":10515,"diff_sha":"90c63f366752eee2594932158e969a48f7e9bd8a5f419495e31ffda7f939c6fc","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":402.1,"excluded_bytes":2687,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"4e743369688bf9f8","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-research-task-inherits-phase-deps.critic.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261021T175015Z-