{"agent":"fx-phase-deps","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"Defaulting this knob to `True` makes the still-unsound `_glob_is_docs` predicate active for every schedule without any user opt-in. For example, with `[gates].doc_globs = [\"docs/x*\"]` and a task whose `globs = [\"docs/*\"]`, `_glob_is_docs` returns `True` because it probes only `docs/x`, but `docs/*` also matches `docs/y`, which is not a document glob. With this new default, that task is exempted from `phase.needs` and can be offered before the phase dependencies it must wait on. The previous review already identified this false positive in `_glob_is_docs`; setting the switch to `True` by default turns that classification bug into the default scheduling behavior.","digest":"512de4e989fd7b15","location":"ddflow/config_sections/schedule.py:192 docs_ignore_phase_needs","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/config_sections/schedule.py:192 docs_ignore_phase_needs"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"With `[gates].doc_globs = [\"docs/**/*.md\"]` and a research task `globs = [\"docs/**/research.md\"]`, every path the task glob can match (for example `docs/foo/research.md`) is also matched by the doc glob, so the task is docs-only and should be exempt from inherited phase `needs`. But `_glob_is_docs(\"docs/**/research.md\", [\"docs/**/*.md\"])` returns `False`: the doc glob is not an exact match, does not end in `/**`, is not `dir/*`, and does not start with `**/`; the fallback `return not any(c in glob for c in \"*?[\") and any(...)` is skipped because the task glob contains `*`. As a result `_docs_only_exempt` returns `False`, `inherited_deps` still adds the phase's ancestor deps, and the docs-only task remains blocked, so the bug is not fixed for this valid doc-glob configuration.","digest":"5ac9e0b0679eaf14","location":"ddflow/core/schedule.py:_glob_is_docs","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/schedule.py:_glob_is_docs"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage"